title: workday_coby_crew_4_HelmeppoWrap
location: ship
---

-> (Available if you haven't yet teamed up with Coby) Okay, let's talk about weatherproofing. //HOW DO??
    <<jump workday_coby_crew_4_Coby_training>>
-> (Available if you haven't yet teamed up with Drake) Maybe I better learn about blizzards next... //HOW DO??
    <<jump workday_coby_crew_4_Drake_training>>
-> (Available if you've already done both) Well, I think we learned a lot today. //HOW DO??
    <<jump workday_coby_crew_4_End>>
===

title: workday_coby_crew_4_Drake_training
location: ship
---

Drake: Blizzards are dangerous, but if you know how to handle them, you'll be fine. We just need to be aware of our circumstances and stay prepared.
-> What if we're not prepared?
    <<set $wdcc4D_points +=1>>
    <<set $wdcc4H_points -=1>>
    Drake: Excellent question. We'll cover that as we go.
    Helmeppo: You should always be prepared, though.
-> Easier said than done.
    <<set $wdcc4D_points -=1>>
-> How can we be aware of our circumstances if we can't see through the snow?
    Drake: ...
    Coby: What Drake means is, I think, that we should assess things as best we can, especially as it begins to snow harder.
Drake: Whenever you're going somewhere that you can reasonably assume may be cold, you should be sure to bring a coil of strong rope and extra thick clothes and blankets.
-> Why the rope?
    Coby: To haul sticks and other materials for building shelter.
    Drake: Yes, that's a good use for it. However, it's easy to get lost in a snowstorm. Visibility is low and even when it's not, landmarks can be obscured by snowdrifts and with the cloud cover, starlight navigation is impossible.
    -> So you use the rope as a compass?
        Drake: No.
        Drake: You hold it with someone else so you don't get separated.
        <<jump workday_coby_crew_4_Drake_rope>>
    -> If you're with someone, you can both hold onto the rope to make sure you don't get lost.
        Drake: Yes, exactly.
        <<jump workday_coby_crew_4_Drake_rope>>
-> Shouldn't you be wearing warm clothes already?
    Coby: There's lots of variability in the weather out on the Grand Line.
    <<jump workday_coby_crew_4_Drake_cold>>
===

title: workday_coby_crew_4_Drake_cold
location: ship
---

Drake: Temperatures can drop quite rapidly. In fact, you should always have your heat lamp on you in case it gets too cold and your body can't adjust.
Coby: ...**Should** I have a heat lamp?
Helmeppo: You know not everyone's a lizard, right? Most normal humans can regulate their body temperatures well enough, even in the cold. A heat lamp's not a bad idea, I guess, but you might not need it.
Drake looks offended, or at least you think he does.
-> Er, some people do get colder than others, and there might be other cold-blooded zoans in the group.
    <<set $wdcc4D_points +=1>>
-> That's rude, Lieutenant Commander!
    <<set $wdcc4D_points +=1>>
    <<set $wdcc4H_points -=1>>
    Helmeppo: What? It's the truth.
-> Yes, let's try to focus on what's useful for everyone, not just ourselves.
    <<set $wdcc4C_points +=1>>
    Coby: I agree. A big picture view is important.
Helmeppo: If you have a lamp, you can use it to light, or melt the snow, I guess.
Drake: Yes, if you're well-prepared with just your warm clothes, it's not a bad idea to repurpose the lamp.
-> Or if you bring too many clothes, could you use them to build a shelter?
    Drake: I suppose if it's that warm... Though perhaps not if it's windy enough to make a difference...
-> Couldn't you share clothes, too? You know, huddle together under them for warmth? *Eyebrow waggle* //HOW DO?? (+1 Drake if you already went on multiple of Drake's dates, -1 Drake otherwise)
    Drake: ...
-> What if we need both the lamp and the clothes to keep warm?
    Drake: You don't want to start sweating in the cold. You should be careful.
Drake: If you do end up with extra clothes that you're not wearing, they can provide extra insulation in your sleeping bag, or they can be tied to the end of the rope to lengthen it.
-> Shouldn't you be bringing a long enough coil of rope?
    <<set $wdcc4D_points -=1>>
    Drake: Yes, but lengthening it may be desirable.
-> Why?
Drake: The primary purpose of the rope is to ensure the whole party stays together. If you're all holding on to the same rope, then even if you can't see or hear one another due to the snow, you won't get lost.
-> If you don't know where you are, aren't you already lost?
    <<set $wdcc4D_points -=1>>
    <<set $wdcc4H_points +=1>>
    Helmeppo: Technically, {$name} **is** right...
-> Wow, I hadn't thought of that!
    <<set $wdcc4D_points +=1>>
Drake: And you can tie a spare shirt to the rope to give yourself a better handle as well.
Coby: Wouldn't a scarf work, too?
-> I like that idea.
    <<set $wdcc4C_points +=1>>
-> But you'll be wearing your scarves.
    <<set $wdcc4D_points +=1>>
    Coby: Ah, that's true...
-> Or another rope, if you have one?
    <<set $wdcc4H_points +=1>>
    Drake: Yes, that's a good point, but this is in the case that you don't, or you're already using them.
Drake: Here, I'll demonstrate.
He tosses Helmeppo one end of the rope and pulls a crisp dress shirt from his pack.
Drake: Now, {$name}, take this shirt. You should roll it up so that it forms a sort of rope.
You follow his instruction; the shirt rolls up easily.
Drake: Now tie it tightly to the main rope.
You grasp onto the rope. Helmeppo is playing with his end, and Drake is holding the other...and you need to demonstrate a good knot so you don't lead all these new recruits astray.
-> Captain Coby, what knot do you think I should choose?
    <<set $wdcc4C_points +=1>>
    <<set $wdcc4D_points +=1>>
    Coby: Great question. You'll want to use a hitch, since you're tying the shirt to the rope... Do you have enough material to do a clove hitch?
    You nod. There's definitely enough here; Drake's arms are quite long.
-> Well, a knot's a knot. I'll notice if it slips off.
    <<set $wdcc4D_points -=1>>
    Drake: In the snow, it may be too late when you do. I would suggest a rolling hitch.
    You comply with the request. Maybe he's right.
<<jump workday_coby_crew_4_Drake_join>>
===

title: workday_coby_crew_4_Drake_rope
location: ship
---

Drake: It's important, as soon as visibility starts to drop, to get out the rope and make sure everyone stays together.
-> Won't we just look like school kids?
    <<set $wdcc4D_points -=1>>
    Drake: Better to look foolish for a false alarm than the alternative.
-> Does nightfall count?
    Drake: Yes, especially if you risk drawing unwanted attention with a lantern.
-> 100%. What if the visibility is dropping so slowly that you don't notice?
    Drake: You'll notice-—if it stays on that pace you'll have time to prepare. And if not, as soon as you even think it's starting to get harder to see, it's better to be safe than sorry.
Drake: And if you pause or find shelter, then you shouldn't move away without picking the rope back up.
Helmeppo: What if you lose the rope? I think you should bring another just in case...
-> Well, if everyone's prepared, then everyone will have a rope.
    <<set $wdcc4D_points +=1>>
    <<set $wdcc4H_points +=1>>
-> Even so, if you're all holding on and keeping track, then you shouldn't lose it.
    <<set $wdcc4D_points +=1>>
Drake: Yes.
-> What are some other uses for rope?
-> That's it?
    <<set $wdcc4D_points -=1>>
Drake: Rope is instrumental in building a shelter. For instance, you'll need rope to haul your materials to the shelter.
-> How many materials are we talking?
    Drake: It depends on what's available, of course. If the snow's really bad, then it's best to save your energy and dig out a hole in the snow, so you won't need materials at all...
-> What if all the sticks and things are buried in the snow?
    <<set $wdcc4D_points +=1>>
    Drake: Great question. Then you should dig a shelter together in the snow.
Drake: You should refer to your basic training in how to build a shelter, and use what's available.
Helmeppo: Or bring a tent.
Drake: If there's enough snow or wind, pitching a tent might not work.
-> If the weather's good enough to haul branches back to a base, I think we'll be able to put up a tent.
    <<set $wdcc4H_points +=1>>
    Drake: I suppose...but you should know how to deal with a situation where you don't have tents, anyway.
-> Yeah, we could lose pegs and stuff in the snow drifts too.
    <<set $wdcc4D_points +=1>>
Drake: You can also use the rope to tie branches together and keep them in place when you lean them up against a rock or snowdrift. That will keep them from blowing over or away in the wind.
-> So we should use our standard knots, like we're building a raft?
    <<set $wdcc4D_points +=1>>
    Drake: Yes, exactly.
-> What if our hands are really cold? Tying knots could get difficult.
    Coby: That's why you get used to doing things in gloves. It took me a while to get there, though...
Drake: Of course, you should keep some rope once you have the shelter, in case the snow starts to come down hard again and you need to send someone outside.
<<jump workday_coby_crew_4_Drake_join>>
===

title: workday_coby_crew_4_Drake_join
location: ship
---

Coby: What if someone goes out and doesn't come back?
Drake: If you notice them leaving without the rope, immediately call them back.
Helmeppo: What if you don't?
Drake: Stay where you are. You don't want the situation to get worse.
-> Could you send a signal to a companion to lead them back?
    Drake: In the most hazardous conditions, it's just not practical—they won't be able to see the light or hear your voice. But use your judgement.
-> What if you're the one who gets lost?
    Drake: If you can no longer see the shelter or your tracks, you should dig a shelter in the snow.
Some of the recruits are starting to look worried-—this is serious stuff, but you don't want to scare them too much... Looks like you're not the only one who's picking up on this, though.
Coby: Do you want to demonstrate building a shelter for us?
Drake: Yes. Let's do that. I'll focus on snow-and-cold-weather-specific things.
Drake: First, let's talk about the more optimal situation, when there's snow on the ground but it's not coming down too fast to be aware of your surroundings. Then, if we have time, we can talk about digging a shelter in the snow.
Drake: Normally, when building a shelter, you'll be gathering branches and rocks from visible places. However, in the snow, they might be covered and difficult to find.
-> Don't they stick up sometimes?
    <<set $wdcc4D_points +=1>>
    Drake: The smaller the stick and the deeper the snow, the less likely it is—but any suspect lumps in the snow are a great place to start.
-> Well, that doesn't give us anything to go on.
    <<set $wdcc4D_points -=1>>
    Coby: There are other environmental cues you can use, right?
    Drake: Correct.
Drake: The best place to look for sticks and branches is near the bases of trees. That's where they'll fall—and we, heavy snow is more likely to knock down large branches that will buffer you from the weather. Those will mostly be visible, but—here, for instance.
He gestures toward a pile of snow at the base of a tree. You can't see anything special about it. Then, Drake begins to clear away snow with his gloved hands, groping around as if for a light switch in the dark...
Drake: Here.
He pulls up a stick, and you can see the rest of it pulling through the snow—it's pretty long, not too skinny.
-> You'd need an awful lot of those to build a shelter for multiple people.
    <<set $wdcc4D_points -=1>>
    Drake: That's why you should all work together, and why, for this demonstration, we'll all be gathering sticks.
-> Should we bring a shovel to help dig in the snow?
    <<set $wdcc4H_points +=1>>
    Drake: If you can fit one in your pack, that works.
Drake: All right. We've got a lot of trees and snow here. Call me over if you need any questions.
The group of recruits scatters to the trees. You, Coby, and Helmeppo follow suit, Helmeppo a bit reluctantly.
Coby: Oh, this tree looks promising.
-> **Follow Coby**
    Coby: See? I've got two sticks already.
    -> Whoa, nice. Let me join you?
        <<set $wdcc4C_points +=1>>
        Coby: Sure, we can get this whole tree done pretty quickly.
    -> Cool.
        You join him in working in the area around his tree.
-> **Stay where you are**
    You don't want to steal Coby's bounty, and his tree looks like it's got a lot of snow beneath its boughs. It would be nice if you could find a few big branches...
    Nothing looks promising though, so you dig where you are; beneath the snow are a couple of sizeable sticks.
do set_background("park", Fade) //HOW DO??
Drake: Okay, let's regroup.
The group makes its way over to him, sticks in arms. Between you all, it's a pretty good haul—though maybe not enough to build a full shelter.
Drake: Now I'm sure you're all familiar with the shelter-building exercise from basic. If you have some kind of structure—a wall, or even a large tree trunk—you can build your shelter to lean around it. So let's put it together. Coby, can you be in charge of tying the knots in the rope?
Coby: Sure. Meppo, can you organize the sticks? {$name}, can you find us a good wall?
You and Helmeppo nod.
There's a large stone wall, what remains of the old base building before the Marines had to expand, that's an obvious choice. You won't really impress your superiors with that, but Coby and Helmeppo are working fast with the sticks.
{$name}: This wall works, right?
Drake: Yes.
The recruits are helping move the sticks over to the wall, and the first stab at the shelter looks—a little too cozy, frankly, even for five of you to pile in on top of each other.
Goat: Maaaa!
You turn, just in time to get out of the way, as Sengoku's goat comes charging through. It doesn't stop at the shelter and rams right into it, knocking over the sticks. And is that a cracking you heard?
Coby: Oh, no...
-> Bad goat! No, how could you do that to our hard work?
    <<set $wdcc4D_points -=1>>
    The goat ignores you as it disentangles itself from the structure.
-> I guess that's one way to test out the sturdiness, huh...
The goat turns, free of the sticks and rope, and if goats could smile mischievously, this one definitely would be doing so right now.
-> Oh, you.
    Goat: Maaa~!
    The goat walks over you and gently headbutts your leg.
-> Aw, Rear Admiral, it was a good demo...
    <<set $wdcc4D_points +=1>>
    Drake: Thank you. I'm not sure that it was, though.
-> Finally, someone livened things up around here.
    <<set $wdcc4D_points -=1>>
Drake: We're running low on time here...
<<jump workday_coby_crew_4_Drake_wrap>>
===

title: workday_coby_crew_4_Drake_wrap
location: ship
---

-> (Available if you haven't yet teamed up with Coby) Okay, let's talk about weatherproofing. //HOW DO??
    <<jump workday_coby_crew_4_Coby_training>>
